## Round 2 repair content (two original roots, second attempts)

- Bounded stable fail-closed validation
  (`skills/ultra-change/scripts/validate_primary_transfer.cjs`): all receipt,
  ledger, frozen-input, revoked-evidence, and sibling reads now go through the
  worktree-digest tool's exported `streamStableRepositoryFile` — the
  validator's duplicated snapshot code was deleted, not parallelled. Paths are
  validated before any filesystem access (escaping paths are never touched),
  parent chains are ordinary non-symlink directories, leaves open no-follow,
  identities replay, text must be strict UTF-8, and per-file byte ceilings
  apply. Handoff directories stream under an entry ceiling with a final exact
  parent/entry identity replay and hold exactly OFFER.json, optional ACK.json,
  and optional RESULT.json. Live validation fails closed on an unobservable
  HEAD/Git (`git_unavailable`). A newest v2 terminal RESULT is bound in one
  finite coherent observation — digest re-observed once after the manifest and
  frozen-input reads (`subject_changed_during_observation` on movement). A
  newer handoff supersedes an older terminal receipt only for the same
  repository, task identity, and owner-grant decision bytes.
- `experimental_ack` on every delegated ZCode terminal result
  (`bin/delegate-worker.cjs`, `bin/delegate.cjs`): the worker's mechanical
  fields and the cancel-path `failureFromSpec` now carry
  `transport_maturity`, `transport_surface`, and `experimental_ack: true`
  whenever `--ack-experimental` authorized the run — finished, failed,
  cancelled, and interrupted results alike. One operator-visible defect was
  hit and fixed during GREEN: a mistyped `exit_code` reference crashed the
  worker; the delegate suite caught it immediately.
- `skills/ultra-test/scripts/worktree_digest.cjs` additionally exports
  `streamStableRepositoryFile` (digest algorithm and CLI behavior unchanged);
  `skills/ultra-change/references/primary-transfer.md` describes the
  fail-closed contract. No other product surface changed.

